  "academyNote": "For school specific INSET days, please contact the relevant school. Usually, schools have 5 INSET days during the academic year (including the designated days).",
  "localFacts": [
    {
      "fact": "Carmarthenshire fixes one designated INSET day for all its schools at the start of each year: Tuesday 1 September 2026 and Wednesday 1 September 2027. Each school chooses its other INSET days.",
      "source": "https://www.carmarthenshire.gov.wales/home/council-services/education-schools/school-term-dates/"
    },
    {
      "fact": "February half term 2027 is 8 to 12 February, a week earlier than in most of England, and the spring term ends on Friday 19 March, a week before Good Friday.",
      "source": "https://www.carmarthenshire.gov.wales/home/council-services/education-schools/school-term-dates/"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The Easter holidays 2027 run from 22 March to 2 April, a week earlier than in most of England, and the summer term starts on Monday 5 April 2027.",
      "source": "https://www.carmarthenshire.gov.wales/home/council-services/education-schools/school-term-dates/"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The council notes that the Welsh Government intends to legislate to keep a sixth INSET day on an ongoing basis, subject to a ministerial decision after the 2026 Senedd election.",
      "source": "https://www.carmarthenshire.gov.wales/home/council-services/education-schools/school-term-dates/"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The calendar is published subject to any changes from government policy decisions, and the council says it accepts no liability for losses from altered holiday arrangements.",
      "source": "https://www.carmarthenshire.gov.wales/home/council-services/education-schools/school-term-dates/"
    }
  ],
